{"id":1116,"date":"2020-11-20T21:55:56","date_gmt":"2020-11-21T05:55:56","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1116"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:43","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:43","slug":"build-the-turret-bot","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/build-the-turret-bot\/","title":{"rendered":"Build the Turret Bot"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22162957fd2\" name=\"6a22162957fd2\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build the base<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt two long L-frames to a blueboard with the long ends sticking up in the air. Pay attention to their placement!<\/li>\n<li>Attach two long standoffs next to each other between the two long L-frames, and then attach two long standoffs next to each other at the opposite end of the blueboard.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt the battery box to the second from the bottom holes on the long L-frames.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt a DC motor to the four long standoffs.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1117&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1118&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1119&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22162958102\" name=\"6a22162958102\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build the pivot point<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Remove the black rubber from a wheel and bolt a short standoff to every other spoke. You should have four short standoffs on the wheel.<\/li>\n<li>Attach the wheel to the motor using a black screw. The wheel will stay on without it though!<\/li>\n<li>Bolt a short standoff to every other hole on the horn bracket.\u00a0You should have four short standoffs on the horn bracket.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt the horn bracket to the short standoffs on the wheel.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1120&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1121&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1122&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1123&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22162958167\" name=\"6a22162958167\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build a wider base<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Place two blueboards next to each other. Attach a bolt at each of the four corners, with the bolts on the bottom of the blueboards.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt four short standoffs a hole away from each of the inner corners.<\/li>\n<li>Attach the first base (with the battery box and pivot point) to the four short standoffs you just attached so you have a wider base.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1124&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1125&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221629581c7\" name=\"6a221629581c7\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Connect the Smart Inventor Board<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>On another blueboard, bolt two short L-frames so the ends sticking up are facing the center of the blueboard. Pay attention to their placement!<\/li>\n<li>Bolt two short standoffs to the underside of the blueboard. Again, pay\u00a0attention to their placement!<\/li>\n<li>Use long bolts to attach the Smart Inventor Board to the two short L-frames.<\/li>\n<li>Using the two short standoffs, attach the blueboard with the Smart Inventor Board to the two long L-frames holding the battery box.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1126&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1127&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1128&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1129&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216295821e\" name=\"6a2216295821e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build the turret arm base<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]We know this entire step looks complicated, but we promise it&#8217;s much easier than it looks. As long as you pay attention to placement you&#8217;ll be OK!<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt three 7-hole metal frames to four 10-hole metal frames. It should look a little like a grid when you&#8217;re finished.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt two short L-frames and two long L-frames to the metal frames. The long ends of the long L-frames should be sticking up and facing the center. The ends of the short L-frames should also be facing the center.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1130&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1131&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216295827d\" name=\"6a2216295827d\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build the turret arm<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt a horn bracket to the short L-frame that&#8217;s closest to the edge of the metal frame grid. Don&#8217;t bolt the horn bracket to the other L-frame!<\/li>\n<li>Bolt a 10-hole metal frame and two short standoffs to the horn bracket.<\/li>\n<li>Attach a 7-hole metal frame to the end of the 10-hole metal frame, and then attach a short standoff next to the bolt.<\/li>\n<li>Attach a 10-hole metal frame to the other 10-hole metal frame using the short standoffs.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1132&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1133&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1134&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1135&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221629582d6\" name=\"6a221629582d6\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Combine the motor, arm, wheel, and base<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Use the short standoffs on top of the body&#8217;s horn bracket to attach the turret arm base.<\/li>\n<li>Attach a bolt to the end of the turret arm. This will be a barrel to hold your rubber bands!<\/li>\n<li>Bolt a DC motor to the top of the two long L-frames extending from the turret arm base.<\/li>\n<li>Attach a wheel to your new motor with a black screw. The wheel will stay on without the screw though!<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1136&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1137&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1138&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216295832c\" name=\"6a2216295832c\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Wire the Turret Bot<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]To wire your Turret Bot, place it so the Smart Inventor Board is facing you:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The motor on your right is M1.<\/li>\n<li>The motor on your left is M2.<\/li>\n<li>Attach the motors to their respective spots on the Smart Inventor Board (M1, M2, M3, and M4 are all marked).<\/li>\n<li>Make sure that the red wires are the in the negative position (facing the inside) and that the black wires are in the positive position (facing the outside)!<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1139&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216295836f\" name=\"6a2216295836f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Video<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]This video explains how the Turret Bot works![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=so_hVvFcyX0&#8243; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 10 Build the base [vc_column_text] Bolt two long L-frames to a blueboard with the long ends sticking up in the air. Pay attention to their placement! Attach two&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/build-the-turret-bot\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1746,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1753,1777,1793,1617,423,626,1533,1438,853,144,59,171],"lesson-tag":[2163,2168,2172,2171,2197,2198],"class_list":["post-1116","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-build","lesson-tag-robotics","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","lesson-tag-turret","lesson-tag-turret-bot","module-turret","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1116","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":3,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1116\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":6625,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1116\/revisions\/6625"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1746"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1116"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1116"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=1116"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}